      "name": "False Claims Act",
      "relevance": "Civil liability for knowingly presenting false claims for federal funds. Qui tam actions are filed under seal by counsel (§ 3730(b)). Relator share under § 3730(d): generally 15-25% if the government intervenes, 25-30% if it declines, and up to 10% where the action rests primarily on publicly disclosed information. § 3730(h) protects against retaliation."
