      "name": "False Claims Act: public disclosure bar",
      "relevance": "Qui tam actions based substantially on publicly disclosed information (including federal reports and databases such as USASpending, NPPES and the LEIE) may be dismissed unless the relator is an 'original source' whose independent knowledge materially adds to the public disclosures. Analysis of public data alone may not qualify; consult counsel before filing."
